<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66022" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελί̆-λωτον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Peripl.M.Rubr.</u>
			49
		</span></i>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελί̆-λωτος</span></b> , ὁ, <i><span class="en">
			Sapph.
			<u>Supp.</u>
			25.14
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Thphr.
			<u>HP</u>
			7.15.3
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>melilot,
				Trigonella graeca</i>, a kind of clover, so called from the
			quantity of honey it contained, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἀνθεμώδης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				98
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				627a8
			</span></i>, Thphr.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>king's clover, Trigonella corniculata</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a tree, acc.
			to <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.3.11
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span>: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				897
			</span></i>.]</div>
